{"schemaVersion":1,"id":"reference:50af9972d0387fe6","name":"Gamorrean","source":{"id":"source:reference-50af9972d0387fe6","title":"Gamorrean","revision":18212,"timestamp":"2024-08-25T19:47:40Z","sha256":"09142d52bf84157486d1713506d426b03be2187a3f12886a60ae5bf96bd38d30","url":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?oldid=18212","history":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?title=Gamorrean&action=history"},"article":{"sourceId":"source:reference-50af9972d0387fe6","blocks":[{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Reference Books: ",{"tag":"a","children":["Core Rulebook"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Core_Rulebook"},", ",{"tag":"a","children":["Knights of the Old Republic Campaign Guide"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Knights_of_the_Old_Republic_Campaign_Guide"}]}]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["Gamorreans are green-skinned, porcine creatures native to ",{"tag":"a","children":["Gamorr"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Gamorr","referenceId":"reference:2267314e8963e4ee"},". Their tendency toward violence makes them valued as criminal enforcers; though viewed as mindless brutes, they don't care so long as they are paid to fight.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["Gamorrean civilization revolves around the never-ending wars between their clans. Preferring large melee weapon in combat, many see ranged weapons as cowardly. Males live to fight; females farm, hunt, and manufacture weapons. Inter-clan hatred rarely fades, and anyone hiring Gamorreans should be aware of their clans to avoid infighting.\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h2","children":["Gamorrean Characteristics"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Personality:"]}," Gamorreans are brutish, violent, and proud. They respect physical prowess and have no problem facing death against a foe they feel they are on at least equal footing with.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Physical Description:"]}," Gamorreans average about 1.8 meters tall and 140 kilograms, with thick green skin covering powerful muscles. Close-set eyes, a thick snout, tusks, and small horns give them a distinct look.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Age Groups"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Age_Groups"},":"]}," Gamorreans age at the following stages:\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"table","children":["\n",{"tag":"tbody","children":[{"tag":"tr","children":["\n",{"tag":"th","children":["CHILD\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"th","children":["YOUNG ADULT\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"th","children":["ADULT\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"th","children":["MIDDLE AGE\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"th","children":["OLD\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"th","children":["VENERABLE\n"]}]},"\n",{"tag":"tr","children":["\n",{"tag":"td","children":["1-6 Years\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["7-12 Years\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["13-29 Years\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["30-39 Years\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["40-44 Years\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["45+ Years\n"]}]}]}]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Homeworld:"]}," The preindustrial world of ",{"tag":"a","children":["Gamorr"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Gamorr","referenceId":"reference:2267314e8963e4ee"},".\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Languages:"]}," Gamorreans speak Gamorrean. They have no written version of the language. They can learn to understand, but not speak other ",{"tag":"a","children":["Languages"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Languages","referenceId":"reference:318655cea4bd2096"},".\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Example Names:"]}," Gartogg, Jubnuk, Ortugg, Ugmush, Venorra, Warlug.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Adventurers:"]}," Some Gamorreans leave their homeworld as slaves, but later escape or buy out their contracts. Others sell their contracts, finding employment as bodyguards or enforcers. A Gamorrean is constantly at war; it's only a matter of figuring out who the enemy is. Gamorrean heroes tend to select the ",{"tag":"a","children":["Soldier"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Soldier","referenceId":"reference:f826baa05bef6921"}," class.\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h2","children":["Gamorrean Species Traits"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["Gamorreans share the following Species Traits:\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"ul","children":[{"tag":"li","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Ability Modifiers:"]}," Gamorreans have a +2 bonus to ",{"tag":"a","children":["Strength"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Strength"},", but suffer a -2 penalty to both their ",{"tag":"a","children":["Dexterity"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Dexterity"}," and ",{"tag":"a","children":["Intelligence"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Intelligence"},". Gamorreans possess greater physical power, but have limited agility and intelligence."]},"\n",{"tag":"li","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Medium Size:"]}," As Medium creatures, Gamorreans have no special bonuses or penalties due to their size."]},"\n",{"tag":"li","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Speed:"]}," Gamorreans have a base speed of 6 squares."]},"\n",{"tag":"li","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Bonus Feat:"]}," Gamorreans gain ",{"tag":"a","children":["Improved Damage Threshold"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Improved_Damage_Threshold","referenceId":"reference:ccb956326c7947a0"}," as a bonus ",{"tag":"a","children":["Feat"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Feat"},"."]},"\n",{"tag":"li","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Great Fortitude:"]}," Gamorreans gain a +2 ",{"tag":"a","children":["Species"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Species","referenceId":"reference:56205e12c20fb568"}," bonus to their ",{"tag":"a","children":["Fortitude Defense"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Fortitude_Defense"},", accounting for their great physical resistance."]},"\n",{"tag":"li","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Natively Phonetic:"]}," Gamorreans can learn to understand, read, and write (but not speak) other ",{"tag":"a","children":["Languages"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Languages","referenceId":"reference:318655cea4bd2096"},"."]},"\n",{"tag":"li","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Primitive:"]}," Gamorreans do not gain ",{"tag":"a","children":["Weapon Proficiency (Heavy Weapons)"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Weapon_Proficiency_(Heavy_Weapons)"},", ",{"tag":"a","children":["Weapon Proficiency (Pistols)"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Weapon_Proficiency_(Pistols)"},", or ",{"tag":"a","children":["Weapon Proficiency (Rifles)"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Weapon_Proficiency_(Rifles)"}," as starting ",{"tag":"a","children":["Feats"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Feats","referenceId":"reference:9194ccf56b9cace0"}," at first level, even if their ",{"tag":"a","children":["Class"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Class"}," normally grants them."]},"\n",{"tag":"li","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Weapon Familiarity (",{"tag":"a","children":["Arg'garok"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Arg%27garok","referenceId":"reference:eaf4a0e14a0ce58f"},"):"]}," Gamorreans treat the ",{"tag":"a","children":["Arg'garok"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Arg%27garok","referenceId":"reference:eaf4a0e14a0ce58f"}," as an ",{"tag":"a","children":["Advanced Melee Weapon"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Advanced_Melee_Weapon"},", instead of an ",{"tag":"a","children":["Exotic Weapons (Melee)"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Exotic_Weapons_(Melee)","referenceId":"reference:e0213365f7fdde76"},"."]},"\n",{"tag":"li","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Automatic Languages:"]}," All Gamorreans can speak Gamorrean. They have no written version of the language. In addition, all Gamorreans understand, read, and write (but not speak) Basic."]}]},"\n",{"tag":"h2","children":["Gamorrean Species Feats"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Reference Book: ",{"tag":"a","children":["Rebellion Era Campaign Guide"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Rebellion_Era_Campaign_Guide"}]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["Gamorrean characters have access to the following ",{"tag":"a","children":["Species Feats"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Species_Feats"},". No Species Feats are considered Bonus Feats for any ",{"tag":"a","children":["Heroic Class"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Heroic_Class"},".\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"table","children":["\n",{"tag":"tbody","children":[{"tag":"tr","children":["\n",{"tag":"th","children":["SPECIES FEAT\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"th","children":["BENEFITS\n"]}]},"\n",{"tag":"tr","children":["\n",{"tag":"td","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Increased Resistance"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Increased_Resistance","referenceId":"reference:54d5009f4e816508"},"\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["Gain a bonus to ",{"tag":"a","children":["Fortitude Defense"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Fortitude_Defense"}," when an enemy fails to affect you.\n"]}]},"\n",{"tag":"tr","children":["\n",{"tag":"td","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Primitive Warrior"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Primitive_Warrior","referenceId":"reference:f2a2cc0c8518c1fc"},"\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["Deal +1 die of damage with ",{"tag":"a","children":["Simple Weapons (Melee)"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Simple_Weapons_(Melee)","referenceId":"reference:cd7a4aafaae07eb3"},".\n"]}]},"\n",{"tag":"tr","children":["\n",{"tag":"td","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Quick Comeback"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Quick_Comeback","referenceId":"reference:1ffd2ce6df6d2a32"},"\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["Recover quickly after being moved down the ",{"tag":"a","children":["Condition Track"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Condition_Track"}," by damage.\n"]}]}]}]},"\n","\n","\n","\n\n","\n\n","\n"]}}
